  "notes": "Godan verb (ら row): {交|まじ}わる・{交|まじ}わります\nて-form: {交|まじ}わって\nた-form: {交|まじ}わった\n\nPROVERB:\n{朱|しゅ}に{交|まじ}われば{赤|あか}くなる — \"If you mix with vermilion, you become red.\" Equivalent to \"You are the company you keep\" or \"Bad company corrupts good character.\"\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {交差|こうさ}する: To intersect — more technical and objective. Used for roads and geometry.\n- {付|つ}き{合|あ}う: To associate with, to date — more common in everyday speech for personal relationships.\n- {交|ま}じる: To mix in with, to be blended — emphasizes becoming part of a group rather than mutual interaction.",
